          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "HWPX inventory trusts unbounded file and central-directory metadata\n\nThe HWPX inventory recursively reads each file into memory and trusts EOCD entry count and offsets without validating central-directory bounds, actual entry count, aggregate size, or corpus limits.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Resource exhaustion unbounded hwpx inventory\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nReuse the bounded archive preflight before reading full files, cap corpus/file sizes and entry counts, validate central-directory ranges, and reject malformed metadata."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:d23f6f4b5cb382423abaf8ba5b26399bee172cf2cb7c98c77369735b54846fbb"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "resource-exhaustion.unbounded-hwpx-inventory",
            "confidence": "medium",
            "findingId": "csf_4547b334aef21917c8fae629",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_42d3f08469a2f0118405a3aa",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.unbounded-hwpx-inventory",
          "ruleIndex": 18
        },
