          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Public export work can outlive its distributed admission lease\n\nPublic export routes obtain a 310-second distributed lease but do not propagate request cancellation or enforce a rendering deadline, so disconnected or hung work can continue after admission protection expires.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Resource exhaustion export cancellation gap\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nPropagate request.signal, wrap rendering in a deadline shorter than the lease, abort worker processes, and keep the lease alive until termination is confirmed."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:9935b36fb0832903cb7b9354e2c05b20df33c202c8634de582aea5889fb0c0e6"
          },
