          "message": {
            "text": "Credential issuance CLIs print bearer tokens to stdout\n\nThe MCP token and Supabase authentication issuance scripts print full bearer tokens to stdout, where terminal capture, CI logs, wrappers, or command transcripts can retain them.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Credential exposure token stdout\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-532, CWE-522\n\nRemediation:\nRequire an explicit reveal flag on an interactive TTY or write the token to a permission-restricted file/credential store; emit only metadata by default."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:664f79864703475999654d0ef42452bca6b17540bddcf5bd938179ec8d8b5397"
