          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Tenant-writable rows can forge authoritative workflow evidence\n\nOwner FOR ALL policies permit direct Data API writes to workflow evidence, including acknowledgement-style rows, bypassing server routes that enforce recipient contact and lifecycle semantics.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Authorization bypass client writable authoritative state\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-602, CWE-862\n\nRemediation:\nApproval-gated: revoke client writes to authoritative evidence tables, expose narrowly scoped server or SECURITY DEFINER transitions, and validate immutable actor and lifecycle fields."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:5db396cc4759bc021d807c1071a143b6c26659b12341ac55efbd0a0951018667"
