          "message": {
            "text": "Public Share uses database object identifiers as bearer credentials\n\nThe public Share GET accepts sessionId plus workerId as the capability and returns session content without recipient contact verification; leakage or enumeration of both identifiers grants access.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Authorization bypass share object ID\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-639\n\nRemediation:\nUse a dedicated high-entropy, revocable public token stored as a hash, bind it to the intended recipient and expiry, and keep contact verification for acknowledgement writes."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
